{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Blessings.</b> HaShem brings upon the head of the righteous." "Another interpretation: <b>Blessings upon the head of the righteous</b> — in life." "<b>And the memory of the righteous is for blessing</b> — after his death." "<b>Covers.</b> Hides violence, so that it does not separate it from him, like יכחידנה תחת לשונו (it hides it under his tongue). And the meaning: he conceals evil. And likewise: פי רשע יבלע און (the mouth of the wicked swallows iniquity)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:50.577553906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}